This software is provided by Aris Vardakas ("the Licensor") for both personal and commercial use. By downloading, installing, and using this software, Fixyfier, on any device that you own or control, you agree to be bound by the terms and conditions of this license agreement.

Data Collection and Usage: Fixyfier does not collect, store, or transmit any personal information to the Licensor. The application runs locally on your device, contains no telemetry or analytics, and gathers no identifiable data for the Licensor's use. Your preferences — such as the theme, the selected language, the confirmation setting, and a small indicator of whether the optional in-app product is owned — are stored locally on your own device, in your user's registry key and application data folder, and are never transmitted. Where Fixyfier interacts with the Microsoft Store to verify ownership of the optional in-app product described below, that interaction is handled entirely by the Microsoft Store and returns only a confirmation of whether the current account owns the product; no personal, account, or payment information is accessed by, or made available to, the Licensor. The Licensor complies with all relevant privacy laws and regulations. At most once a day, and whenever you click the version number, Fixyfier asks the Microsoft Store whether a newer version of the application is available to you; only when one is does it download the published change log from fixyfier.com, to show you what is new. Neither request includes any personal information.

Purchases and In-app Products: Fixyfier is free to use. It offers a single optional, one-time in-app purchase, "Support the Developer", which unlocks the MyTools feature described below. Before buying, you may run your own scripts a limited number of times at no cost; the count of those free runs is kept locally on your device and nowhere else. The purchase is entirely optional, and every other feature works identically whether or not it is bought. Purchases are processed exclusively through the Microsoft Store using your Microsoft account. All payment, billing, and account information is handled by Microsoft under the Microsoft Store Terms of Sale and the Microsoft Privacy Statement, and is never received or stored by the Licensor. To determine whether the feature should be unlocked, Fixyfier asks the Microsoft Store whether your account owns the product and stores only a small, non-personal ownership indicator locally on your device; this indicator contains no personal information and is not transmitted to the Licensor.

Your Own Scripts (MyTools): The MyTools feature lists the script files you place in your own MyTools folder and starts them when you ask it to. Those files are yours: the Licensor does not supply, read, inspect, modify, or vouch for them, cannot determine whether any of them is safe, and cannot reverse what one does. Because Fixyfier runs with administrator rights, any script started from it runs with the same rights and can change anything on your device. You are solely responsible for the files you place in that folder, for your decision to run them, and for every consequence of running them. Run only files that you wrote yourself or that you fully trust.

Third-party Cleaning Rules: The Extra Cleaning Rules feature reads winapp2.ini, a cleaning rule set maintained by the winapp2 project and made available under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International license. That file is not written by, supplied by, or checked by the Licensor. It is downloaded from the winapp2 project when you ask for it, held in memory for as long as you are looking at it, and never stored on your device; alternatively, it is read from a copy you have placed there yourself. Fixyfier shows you which rules apply to this device, shows you the exact files, folders and registry values each selected rule would remove, and removes nothing until you have seen that list and agreed to it. The Licensor does not endorse any individual rule, cannot determine whether removing a given item is appropriate for your device, and cannot reverse a removal. Your selection, and every consequence of it, is yours. The winapp2 project is not affiliated with, and does not endorse, Fixyfier.

Data Security: Although Fixyfier does not collect personal data, the Licensor is committed to maintaining high standards of security, including encryption and regular updates, to ensure the software operates securely on your device.

